# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# kernel-slim.config: daily K3 minus what the SM8250 phone never uses.
#
# Merged on top of the daily .config (~/android/build/k3-daily/.config,
# which already carries device/instantnoodlep/kernel.config) with
# scripts/kconfig/merge_config.sh -m + olddefconfig; built as branch
# instantnoodlep-k3-slim in ~/src/l-k3-slim. See device/instantnoodlep/
# KERNEL-SIZE.md for the evidence and the ABL rule that motivates this.
#
# Why: every kernel whose arm64 header image_size (offset 0x10) is above
# the ABL boundary (~0x2b60000..0x2b70000 on this unit) hangs in ABL before
# USB comes up; the target is image_size <= 0x2560000 (6 MiB below
# 0x2b60000). Only =y symbols change the Image; =m objects stay modules
# and are not touched. DEBUG_INFO is left on: it only bloats vmlinux's
# non-alloc debug sections, never the loaded Image.
#
# Keep list (do not disable): panel/DSI (DRM_MSM*), s6sy761 touch, GENI
# i2c/spi/uart, GPU (DRM_MSM/freedreno), Wi-Fi/BT (ath11k/hci_qca as
# modules), bq27411 gauge, USB dwc3 gadget (NCM/ACM), UFS (SCSI_UFS_QCOM
# + QMP UFS PHY), PCIe, SMMU, MHI/WWAN, CAMSS/IMX471, probe initramfs
# needs (DEVTMPFS, INITRD, PSTORE_RAM, QCOM_WDT, PON, PM8941 pwrkey).

# --- Identify the build ---
# uname -r must differ from the daily kernel so a RAM boot is unambiguous.
CONFIG_LOCALVERSION="-instantnoodlep-k3-slim"

# --- Symbol tables (`.rodata`, the biggest chunk of the image) ---
# KALLSYMS_ALL puts every data symbol into kallsyms_names; daily's .rodata is 15.1 MiB, the bulk of it kallsyms. KALLSYMS=y keeps function names in oops, so panic debugging keeps working.
# CONFIG_KALLSYMS_ALL is not set

# --- Other SoC platforms (arm64 defconfig turns every ARCH_* in arch/arm64/Kconfig.platforms on) ---
# instantnoodlep is qcom,sm8250 only. ARCH_* gates the mediatek/meson/hisi/rockchip/stm32/tegra/exynos/... clk, pinctrl, phy, regulator, mfd, soc, ufs and net drivers that are built in today (several MiB of .text).
